{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeH3AlgebraLaws","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeH3AlgebraLaws","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.MarkovTraceOnHecke"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.trM₂_cyclic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.trM₂_cyclic","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH3AlgebraLaws.lean#L165-L170","doc":"The level-2 trace is cyclic for the rank-one product (H₂ is\ncommutative): packaged for the eventual `MarkovTrace` instance at n=2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.trM_iota23_stabilizes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.trM_iota23_stabilizes","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH3AlgebraLaws.lean#L155-L163","doc":"**Bottom rung of the Markov stabilization** (Tier-2 base case):\nthe level-3 trace restricts to the level-2 trace along the inclusion,\n`trM(ι x) = trM₂ x`. Together with the already-proved Markov reduction\n`trM_markov_σ₁` (`tr(x·σ₁) = z·tr(x)` for `x ∈ H₂`), this is the complete\nconcrete content of the `n = 2 → 3` stabilization step. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.iota23_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.iota23_mul","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH3AlgebraLaws.lean#L146-L153","doc":"**The inclusion is multiplicative**: `iota23` carries the H₂ product\n`(a₁ + b₁σ)(a₂ + b₂σ) = (a₁a₂ + b₁b₂) + (a₁b₂ + b₁a₂ + h·b₁b₂)σ` (the\nHecke quadratic in rank one) to the H₃ NF product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.trM₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.trM₂","kind":"def","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH3AlgebraLaws.lean#L142-L144","doc":"The level-2 Markov trace: `trM₂(a·γ + b·σ₀) = a + z·b`\n(weights `(1, z)`, the `n = 2` row of the Markov–Ocneanu–Wenzl weights). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.iota23","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.iota23","kind":"def","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH3AlgebraLaws.lean#L139-L140","doc":"The `H₂ ↪ H₃` inclusion on NF coordinates: `a·γ + b·σ₀ ↦ (a,b,0,0,0,0)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.mulNF_assoc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.mulNF_assoc","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH3AlgebraLaws.lean#L118-L129","doc":"**Associativity of the full H₃(q) NF product**: `(u·v)·w = u·(v·w)`.\nThe load-bearing algebra-object law — a polynomial identity in the 18\nentries and `h`, closed by `ring` per entry after unfolding the nested\n`mulσ` actions (same discipline as `trM_cyclic`; the operator table was\npinned by the symbolic preflight in `gram.py` and cross-verified over\n`ℚ(z,h)`). With bilinearity and the unit laws above, the NF module is an\nassociative unital R-algebra — the concrete algebra object of the braided\nsource category. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.mulNF_one_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.mulNF_one_left","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH3AlgebraLaws.lean#L111-L116","doc":"**Left unit law**: `γ · v = v` — each basis word applied to γ reproduces\nthe corresponding NF basis element (`word_j(γ) = b_j`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.mulNF_one_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.mulNF_one_right","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH3AlgebraLaws.lean#L105-L109","doc":"**Right unit law**: `u · γ = u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.unitNF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.unitNF","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH3AlgebraLaws.lean#L102-L103","doc":"The unit of the NF algebra: γ = e₀ = `![1,0,0,0,0,0]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.mulNF_smul_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.mulNF_smul_right","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH3AlgebraLaws.lean#L95-L100","doc":"`mulNF` is R-homogeneous in the right factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.mulNF_smul_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.mulNF_smul_left","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH3AlgebraLaws.lean#L88-L93","doc":"`mulNF` is R-homogeneous in the left factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.mulNF_add_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.mulNF_add_right","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH3AlgebraLaws.lean#L82-L86","doc":"`mulNF` is additive in the right factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.mulNF_add_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.mulNF_add_left","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH3AlgebraLaws.lean#L76-L80","doc":"`mulNF` is additive in the left factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.braid_operator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.braid_operator","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH3AlgebraLaws.lean#L64-L72","doc":"**The braid relation** `σ₀σ₁σ₀ = σ₁σ₀σ₁` as an operator identity on the\nNF module — the Yang–Baxter / braiding-hexagon shadow (the F2 datum of the\n`HeckeBraidedPresentation`), machine-checked at the concrete n=3 rung. All\nthree presentation field contents are now realized at n=3 (far commutation\nis vacuous with two generators). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.mulσ₁_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.mulσ₁_hecke","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH3AlgebraLaws.lean#L55-L62","doc":"**Hecke quadratic for σ₁** — partner of the existing `mulσ₀_hecke`:\n`σ₁² = h·σ₁ + 1` as an operator identity on the NF module. With this, BOTH\ngenerators satisfy the R-matrix eigenvalue equation concretely. ","signatureChunk":0}]}